SM(275,{"n":"Genesis 49-50","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Genesis 49-50.mp3","d":2328.1,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.4,"Chapter 49. Now Jacob called his sons and said, Gather together that I may tell you what shall befall you in the last days."],[28.8,"Just a comment on that phrase, because that is accurately translated from the Greek."],[32.88,"The last days."],[34.18,"That's how it's usually translated Greek, but occurs in the New Testament."],[37.86,"But how do people read it in the New Testament?"],[43.06,"Last days. Yes, that's the second coming."],[45.54,"That's the Armageddon."],[47.08,"That's the Apocalypse."],[47.96,"That's the end of the world."],[49.08,"This is clearly not talking about the end of the world."],[52.77,"A better, a better translation of this is actually latter days."],[58.69,"People don't want to use that anymore because of the Mormons"],[63.45,"But latter days meaning like not tomorrow, like down the road."],[69.26,"Verse 2 gather together and hear, you sons of Jacob, and listen to Israel your father."],[75.18,"Reuben, you are my firstborn, my might and the beginning of my children."],[78.94,"You are hard to bear."],[80.7,"You are hardened in your self will."],[83.9,"Unstable as water in your insolence."],[86.7,"You went up to your father's bed, then you defiled it."],[93.1,"Kind of happened."],[94.4,"So he points out."],[95.86,"This is clearly concerning his son."],[98.44,"But there are elements of the character of his son."],[101.24,"We'll see more of the tribe of Reuben later"],[101.92,"Stubborn, strong-willed. And we'll uh comment on this."],[112.16,"Verse 5, Simeon and Levi are brothers."],[115.76,"They accomplished their injustice from their free choice."],[119.2,"Let not my soul enter their counsel, let not my honor be united to their assembly."],[124.08,"For in their anger they slew a man, and in their self will they hamstrung an ox."],[129.04,"Cursed be their anger, for it was self-willed, and their wrath, for it was hardened."],[133.76,"I will divide them in Jacob and scatter them in Israel."],[139.76,"That sounds mean."],[140.89,"But again, this is referring to wait, now Shechem's bad again."],[150.66,"But now we get to Judah."],[152.6,"So now we're past disinherited people."],[156.84,"Judah, you are he whom your brothers shall praise."],[159.64,"Your hand shall be on the neck of your enemies."],[163.0,"Your father's sons shall bow down before you."],[167.72,"Judah is a lion's cub."],[170.12,"From being a shoot, my son, you have grown up."],[174.92,"He bows down and slept as a lion and a cub, and who shall rouse him?"],[181.32,"Pause for a second."],[183.96,"Couple things. So now we have this idea of the brothers bowing down to him."],[190.08,"Remember, that was Joseph in the dream."],[192.78,"So sometimes when we get these prophetic utterances."],[196.51,"This the idea is, as St."],[198.51,"Peter's gonna say later, no prophecy is founded in the will of man."],[201.4,"It comes with the Holy Spirit."],[203.69,"So what we're seeing here is Judah does have this firstborn status."],[210.65,"Whether that's who Jacob wants to designate or not."],[215.34,"And that's gonna play out, of course, as we know."],[218.22,"There's the old testament."],[221.34,"Yes. Yes. But notice it's not as obvious in Reuben, but you got the ox and Simeon and Levi."],[231.02,"There's gonna be a lot of animal imagery."],[232.54,"That's yes This is related to the Zodiac, I agree."],[239.54,"So each of the constellations, as they were understood in the ancient Near East by Hebrew people, is going to be lined up with one of the twelve tribes."],[251.54,"So yeah, let's comment on Jewish astrology."],[255.3,"And these are symbols, that are going to be and are going to be present not just prophetically, but in a very literal way, like in the high priest's garment, he's going to have stones with these constellations on them in his ephod when he goes into the temple."],[271.96,"So, you know, I know we've all been taught astrology bad."],[275.82,"Or in our modern world, more often astrology dumb."],[279.83,"Um yes, newspaper astrology is mostly just dumb, not so much evil."],[286.65,"I'm gonna make vague, today's a good day to make, you know, it's like a fortune cookie."],[291.31,"Like um, yeah, today's a good day to take advantage of opportunities, you know, like just this sort of vague nonsense."],[302.01,"Uh but so the the the issue of astrology, and there is no real astronomy in the ancient world as we know it today."],[315.45,"Uh the issue of astrology is different than we tend to think about it."],[319.41,"Because for everybody, and we talked about this with Abraham with the stars."],[323.86,"For everybody in the ancient Near East and the ancient world pretty much entirely, the sun and moon and stars were seen as divine, as at least small g gods, even by Jewish people."],[337.63,"As these spiritual beings."],[338.83,"So they're like identical with the angels, sort of all through the Bible, stars and angels, but even in the New Testament."],[344.69,"Are connected in this way."],[346.93,"As we saw even in Revelation, for example."],[352.09,"The difference is, and Philo lays this out, Philo of Alexandria, who's a first century BC Jewish author."],[359.77,"He says, here's the difference between Moses and you guys, you pagans."],[363.67,"You pagans see these small g gods."],[367.13,"These gods, the heavens, and you think they're sort of ultimate in their own right."],[372.89,"You think they're to be worshipped, you think they have power, they control your destiny, they control the future."],[380.55,"Which is what actual like occult astrology is, like the start to determine what's going to happen."],[386.56,"He says, you right, think that."],[389.65,"But in reality, he says, we know that these are angels, these are messengers of God."],[398.07,"That these are servants of God."],[400.95,"So Jewish astrology, and we'll just go ahead and call it that."],[405.97,"Jewish astrology, the astrology of Israel, of the Old Testament, was about the idea that the heavens, what was going on in the heavens, could communicate, God could communicate things to us through that."],[424.98,"Since it's just past Christmas."],[427.23,"God could communicate, for example, that the Messiah had been born through a star appearing in a certain constellation at a certain time."],[437.84,"Not that that star was a god that caused blah blah blah blah blah."],[443.38,"But communication. Messenger."],[446.44,"When we get to that psalm, that psalm is all about astrology"],[446.88,"The heavens proclaim the glory of God."],[452.4,"There's literally astrological terms in it."],[455.92,"It talks about the horizon divide and the zodiac and stuff."],[459.12,"We'll talk about it."],[460.56,"But um, that it can communicate is the idea."],[466.96,"And so this connection of the twelve tribes to the constellations in the heavens is this idea that the people God's people."],[477.62,"The people of Israel are like part of the whole workings of the cosmos."],[482.98,"Well, that isn't a blessing."],[484.15,"It'll be like the heavens."],[485.51,"Yeah, like the stars of the heavens."],[487.45,"So there is this connection."],[489.21,"They're not supposed to worship them"],[489.37,"They're not supposed to. think they interpret their destiny"],[494.71,"But God could speak through his creation."],[499.03,"This is the understanding."],[500.55,"So, and we'll get in."],[501.75,"There's lots of places where astrological stuff shows up in the Old Testament."],[506.39,"We're just kind of inured to it."],[508.07,"Like Ezekiel's vision, a lot of the four living creatures is about astrology."],[513.43,"Babylonian astrology. But we'll get there in a few years."],[519.75,"But for right now, yeah."],[521.19,"So this is related to those symbols, which are not identical."],[525.27,"They're very similar."],[526.65,"So, like what we would now call a constellation Leo is the same lion."],[530.35,"But some of them are a little different."],[532.75,"Um Scorpio, a lot of times in ancient astrology was a dragon."],[539.99,"Just as an example."],[540.95,"They didn't see it as a scorpion, they saw it as a dragon."],[544.23,"I mean, if you've ever seen the actual console."],[547.47,"You got some freedom in terms of how you're gonna how you're gonna understand uh and interpret these."],[553.39,"So and that's why this is where the lion becomes sort of the little Judah."],[558.27,"Verse 10 the scepter shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from his loins until Shiloh comes, and to him shall be the expectation of the nations."],[570.27,"Binding his colt to a vine and his donkey's colt to its branch, he will wash his garments in wine and his clothes in the blood of grapes."],[578.51,"es. His ey are gladdened from the wine, and his teeth are whiter than milk"],[586.31,"So this is not the first messianic prophecy."],[590.31,"We saw the first messianic prophecy all the way back in Genesis 3 about the seed of the woman."],[596.31,"And how interesting that language is, since technically speaking, women don't have seed."],[601.72,"But this is one of the very early."],[604.38,"And this identifies him with the tribe of Judah for the first time."],[610.14,"This messianic figure."],[611.58,"Why do I say Messianic figure?"],[613.1,"Well, Mashiach, means the anointed one."],[615.94,"The king. King is all over this."],[620.11,"Scepter. This is there's gonna be a king, and it's not gonna depart until Shiloh comes."],[620.93,"That's rather vague"],[628.17,"Yeah, but on earth."],[629.54,"There's gonna be this coming."],[631.12,"What is Shiloh?"],[633.04,"Well, it's a place."],[637.2,"Yeah. Where Samuel the prophet is going to be, but what does it mean until a city comes?"],[643.52,"Yeah, that's weird."],[645.04,"Yeah, yeah. And this is gonna be understood to be talking about so the coming of the Messiah, and then in Christian interpretation, the second coming of the Messiah."],[657.33,"But this is gonna get interpreted through Psalm 110, which we'll get to in a couple years, and go into that in detail."],[662.93,"But yeah, yeah."],[663.65,"So this is one building block."],[664.05,"We're still in Genesis"],[667.88,"But these ideas and these concepts, the understanding of God we've already seen, the understanding of the Messiah."],[673.0,"This is getting built before we even get into Exodus and the Torah proper."],[679.1,"These concepts are already getting starting to get built up."],[683.34,"Is it uh going into what this vine and its branch means?"],[688.62,"Yeah, remember when Jesus gets the uh cold?"],[693.82,"Yeah. And it quotes that."],[696.14,"But what's it what does it mean here?"],[699.18,"Well, here it's cryptic prophecy."],[701.5,"Okay. It's literally a cryptic reference."],[707.69,"Because now a later prophet is going to do something with this, but it's gonna be several years before we get to Zechariah."],[715.21,"Um but uh there's the the symbolism here is odd at the time."],[724.41,"Because on one hand this person's being described as a king, and now he's being described as riding a donkey's cult that he ties up himself."],[734.33,"Some reference to certain."],[735.85,"So there's there's this there's this juxtaposition here, and that later prophet we get there is gonna play up that juxtaposition."],[745.66,"Of royalty and humility, which are two things that do not normally go together at all ever."],[752.6,"But beyond that, there's not like a clear direct meaning."],[756.54,"Okay. It's sort of poetic and sort of just this imagery that doesn't seem to go together."],[761.9,"Any more than the covenant of Shiloh."],[764.7,"And he will wash his garments in wine and his clothes of the blood of grapes."],[768.62,"Well that makes actually that kind of makes sense."],[770.88,"It's because it's royal, royal purple."],[773.6,"That'll make it purple, but it doesn't say die, it says wash."],[777.62,"But then you so you have that ambiguous double meaning with the you know, the actual blood crisis."],[782.28,"Yeah. Yeah. But the idea of washing in blood."],[788.5,"Not he will die it purple."],[790.34,"But but I mean. royalties of washing"],[793.9,"You don't wash something by putting wine all over it."],[797.95,"We would call that a stain."],[800.28,"So there's a juxtaposition there too."],[803.1,"There's these ideas that would seem to be they're put in parallel what they were."],[809.24,"That that don't seem to logically fit together."],[812.74,"And his eyes are gladdened from the wine and his teeth are whiter than milk."],[819.3,"So when when we get to the New Testament, there's something that kind of gets overplayed a lot of times in our reading, and that is Christ will say things like Christ on the road to Obeas."],[831.06,"Explains the things in all the scriptures concerning himself"],[837.8,"And we what tends to get overplayed is this idea that, like, oh, no one could have possibly understood what was said in the Old Testament about the Messiah until Jesus explained it to them."],[850.38,"And I got bad news, there are a lot of people who did."],[853.1,"You can read Second Temple Jewish literature."],[856.62,"We wouldn't expect them otherwise."],[858.56,"But there are elements of the prophecy."],[860.8,"The idea that's being gotten at is once you see who Christ is and what he does, then these things that seem like weird juxtapositions make sense."],[871.69,"They come together."],[872.99,"Like you were talking about Christ's blood at his garments"],[876.63,"Now this washing with blood."],[879.56,"Now I see."],[880.6,"Okay, yeah. There you go."],[884.1,"So what was a sort of cryptic messianic prophecy."],[887.96,"So later a prophet could say, look, he's a king, he's coming on a donkey."],[891.8,"This has to do with humility."],[894.92,"So the Messiah is going to come with humility."],[897.17,"There are people who had worked that much out."],[900.26,"But even then, once you see Christ, the life he lived."],[903.56,"The humility, once you understand Christ's divine nature and his humiliation."],[909.72,"Okay. It all comes together, it all comes together."],[914.54,"But here, this is a almost a riddle"],[920.65,"And there's no way, if these words are being spoken to the historical person, Judah, that he has any idea what this means."],[928.41,"Other than, well, okay, I guess a king is gonna be descended from great, cool."],[934.09,"A long dynasty of kings."],[936.25,"Groovy, that's good."],[938.95,"Yeah, yeah, like that's that's great, okay."],[942.63,"Uh, but beyond that, like the details of this would clearly not be apparent to that man standing there that day."],[950.71,"Okay, verse 13."],[952.23,"Zebulin shall dwell by the sea coast, he shall be near a haven for ships and his, border shall adjoin adjoin Sidon."],[956.95,"So Zebulun just gets told where his descendants are gonna live"],[963.15,"That's kind of the short end of this deck."],[965.07,"Issachar desired what was good, resting between the inheritances, and seeing his resting place was good and the land was fertile, he set his shoulder to hard work and became a farmer."],[977.31,"So tribe named after you are gonna be farmers."],[983.55,"See there's different levels of excitement here."],[985.87,"Is that also potentially connecting to the Ezra Nehemiah?"],[990.19,"Like, hey, you guys helped us out, you're Issach."],[992.91,"Yeah, why they picked Issachar, yes."],[995.39,"Yeah, yeah. They could have picked anybody, yeah."],[1000.19,"And also where they were dwelling."],[1001.63,"Yeah But those are related."],[1003.99,"They're dwelling on farmland, they're farming."],[1006.39,"Now, that said, that said, you know, I know I uh was just playing up like, yay, farmers."],[1015.25,"But if you've been living nomadically, having land that you're gonna possess and be able to work, hand on to your descendants to work, that is a promise."],[1026.75,"Yeah. That is a legitimate thing."],[1030.23,"And dwelling on the seacoast and having ports, being involved in car."],[1036.31,"These are legit things."],[1037.91,"I mean, they're definitely not as exciting as having the Messiah."],[1041.72,"But these are legitimate sort of promises."],[1046.45,"And can be seen as that."],[1051.41,"Dan not doesn't do so well here."],[1053.89,"Verse 16: Dan shall judge his own people as one of the tribes of Israel."],[1060.29,"Dan means this is probably not the origin of the word, but Dan in Hebrew means judge or judgment."],[1069.01,"Judgment like condemnation."],[1071.25,"Not judgment like I judge and do equity."],[1074.93,"Like it means I like condemn."],[1079.61,"Uh Dan shall judge his own people as one of the tribes of Israel."],[1083.17,"Dan shall be a serpent by the way, a viper lying in ambush by the path that bites the horse's heels, that its rider may fall backward, waiting for the Lord's salvation."],[1097.07,"So you can imagine the actual person, Dan saying they're going, What'd I do?"],[1101.25,"Like, and again, it's not talking about him."],[1105.27,"A person, it's talking about what's gonna happen with the tribe of Dan, which is gonna be nothing good."],[1110.79,"So we're gonna get really upset about me pointing out what the Bible and the church fathers say about Samson."],[1125.83,"But he's not the only place where Dan is a problem."],[1129.11,"Dan is always a problem."],[1130.23,"We talked about this a little bit back in Revelation when, as we mentioned earlier, he gets left out of the new heavens and the new earth."],[1140.85,"That's kind of the final word on you."],[1146.13,"Verse 19, as for Gad, a raider gang shall raid him, but he shall raid them in close pursuit."],[1155.57,"So it's a pirate's life for you."],[1158.13,"You're gonna live by your wits fighting with your neighbors."],[1163.73,"As for Asher, his food shall be abundant, and he will furnish dainties for rulers."],[1168.29,"That's another great translation."],[1170.53,"Let us all go and sup on dainties."],[1176.37,"But abundant food is good."],[1179.14,"And you're going to produce delicacies."],[1181.99,"That's a promise."],[1183.72,"Verse 21, Naphtali is a spreading stem, bestowing beauty by its produce."],[1191.54,"These are nice things."],[1193.62,"Verse 22, Joseph is a grown-up son, a grown-up son that was envied."],[1198.66,"O my youngest son, returned to me."],[1200.82,"They devised evil plans against him and reviled him."],[1203.94,"And the archers were taking aim at him."],[1206.9,"But their bows were broken by force, and the sinews of the arms of their hands were enfeebled, on account of the hand of the mighty one of Jacob."],[1215.7,"Thence he who strengthened Israel is from the God of your father, and my God has helped you and blessed you with a blessing from heaven above, and with a blessing of the earth containing everything."],[1228.14,"By reason of the blessing of breasts and the womb, he made the blessings of your father and mother stronger than the blessings of stable mountains and everlasting hills."],[1236.78,"They shall be on the head of Joseph and on the crown of the brothers he led."],[1242.94,"So no favoritism things."],[1248.0,"And he's presented here as recounting this in front of the brothers who did all that stuff to him."],[1253.52,"But also note again what we said about Ephraimite traditions, and this being here."],[1260.97,"And this being maintained here."],[1262.81,"Benjamin is a ravenous wolf"],[1264.45,"Verse 27. In the morning he will still be eating, and in the evening he will provide food."],[1273.01,"So again, Benjamin's like, what did I do?"],[1278.54,"Well, we'll see what Benjamin does."],[1282.92,"Um. So again, this is not about Benjamin the kid."],[1288.58,"This is about the descendants who are going to come after him, who are going to be a particularly sinister lot."],[1296.98,"That joke is on purpose."],[1298.9,"I'm going to make it a lot."],[1301.46,"Get used to it."],[1303.3,"It's like Sisyphus jokes."],[1305.38,"Great thing about Sisyphus jokes is you can tell the same one over and over, and it just gets funnier each time."],[1311.58,"So I say the sinister joke is, of course, because most of the people of the tribe of Benjamin are going to be left-handed."],[1318.46,"And there's a joke about that in the text."],[1322.3,"Benjamin means son of my right hand."],[1326.22,"And they're going to be left-handed."],[1327.9,"So if you're going to get mad at me for puns, take issue with Moses first."],[1337.7,"But so yeah, we're gonna see what happens with the tribe of Benjamin."],[1343.43,"Um so, like what's said about Judah and what's said about Benjamin here is really explainable by what happens in later history from the perspective of Judah."],[1355.47,"Of what's going to become the nation of Judah."],[1358.27,"But what's said about Joseph here in this chapter is not from that perspective."],[1363.13,"So again, the fact that this has these earlier Ephraimite traditions that are held in parallel with those Judah and Benjamin traditions is a pretty clear pointer to the age, to the antiquity of the core of this text."],[1382.09,"Verse 28 All these are the twelve sons of Israel, and this is what their father spoke to them and blessed them, and he blessed each one according to his own blessing."],[1390.17,"Then he charged them and said to them, I am to be added to my people, bury me with my fathers in the cave of in the field of Ephron the Hittite, opposite Mamre, in the land of Canaan, which Abraham bought from Ephron the Hittite as a possession for a burial place."],[1411.47,"This uh tomb before, this is the one that Abraham bought, as it just said."],[1416.05,"And we already saw him make Joseph promise that he'd be his body would be returned there."],[1421.09,"Notice the language he uses about his death, though."],[1426.45,"I'm about to be added to my people."],[1429.78,"So there are folks who will tell you."],[1433.58,"The whole idea of the resurrection of the dead."],[1438.7,"Uh some will say is a Christian in some like Bart Ehrman will say is a Christian invention."],[1447.18,"That Israelites and Jews did not believe in an afterlife."],[1454.22,"Read the Torah, Bart."],[1456.06,"Uh. But this clearly argues otherwise."],[1460.04,"Because this goes beyond the language that Isaac used."],[1462.92,"I'm gonna go rest with my father."],[1464.44,"That language rests with my fathers."],[1466.22,"Because that you could say, well, that's just metaphorical."],[1468.48,"Like his body is literally resting next to his father's body."],[1471.66,"But added to my people."],[1475.66,"That phrase crops up again in like the book of Kings."],[1479.1,"Yeah, yeah. The idea of being added to my people means I'm going to join them, meaning they are somewhere"],[1487.19,"They are somewhere, and I am going there to join them."],[1492.2,"Not I'm being subtracted from you, but I'm being added to them."],[1497.16,"So that's important language again about the antiquity of that idea."],[1501.18,"That understanding. And it's because that's how he sees his death."],[1511.1,"It's because he sees that as rejoining his people."],[1515.42,"His father, his grandfather, his mother, his grandmother, his wives who have predeceased him."],[1522.62,"Because he sees it that way, he wants them to bury his body with them."],[1530.58,"This is a connection sometimes people have trouble with."],[1532.74,"I get a lot of questions about why in the Orthodox Church we don't let people be cremated."],[1538.31,"And I say it's because of our belief in the resurrection."],[1543.11,"It's because we believe that when we die, we're being added to our people."],[1548.23,"That we take our body and put it with our people."],[1555.83,"That's why. Because we don't see death as, oh good, now I'm, you know, one bright morning when this life is over, I'll fly away."],[1566.17,"Leave this body, leave this world behind"],[1566.28,"That's not what we believe"],[1568.9,"Don't need it anymore."],[1572.08,"If we believe that, then sure."],[1573.84,"Take it and burn it."],[1574.8,"Who cares? Verse 31, there they buried Abraham and Sarah his wife."],[1585.52,"There they buried Isaac and Rebekah his wife."],[1588.24,"And there I buried Leah."],[1590.56,"The field and the cave there were purchased from the sons of Het."],[1595.92,"Notice what's interesting."],[1597.6,"He gets buried with Leah."],[1599.36,"Rachel Not Rachel."],[1604.36,"Thus, when Jacob finished commanding his sons, he drew his feet up into the bed and breathed his last and was added to his people."],[1615.48,"So he dies."],[1616.92,"And notice again, we're very clear."],[1619.08,"It is made very clear over and over again in Genesis where this place is."],[1625.08,"In the case of Rachel, who's buried separately, where that place is."],[1633.4,"People go there."],[1636.12,"They go to where they're buried."],[1638.22,"They go on pilgrimages to these places and pray there."],[1642.96,"And they still do, yes."],[1645.52,"From three different religions, they still do."],[1647.86,"But. They go there."],[1650.54,"So again. This idea of relics, this idea of shrines, this idea of going to bare places and praying."],[1653.18,"This is not a new thing in Christianity"],[1659.86,"Definitely not in medieval Roman Catholicism."],[1662.58,"But it's not even a new thing in Christianity."],[1664.98,"This is embedded here in the Torah."],[1668.32,"That one of the things, when Israel comes out of Egypt to the rest of the Torah and comes back into the land, one of the things they're now able to do when they come back into the land is return to these places where their fathers and forefathers are buried."],[1685.92,"To the altars that they built."],[1688.64,"To Yahweh their God."],[1690.32,"That's part of what's happening in the Exodus that I think we kind of lose"],[1694.58,"Because we've lost a sense of sort of sacred places and sacred space in Western culture to a large extent."],[1702.04,"Being able to go back to those places, is a powerful thing."],[1706.42,"Chapter 50. Now Joseph fell on his father's face and wept over him and kissed him."],[1711.22,"And Joseph commanded his servants, the physicians, to embalm his father."],[1715.62,"So the physicians embalmed Israel."],[1717.7,"Forty days were required for him."],[1719.94,"For such are the days required for those embalmed, and the Egyptians mourned for him seventy days."],[1729.3,"Yeah. So why did he have a bin balm, though?"],[1731.62,"Because he's planning to take his remains back."],[1737.34,"To uh Canaan."],[1740.06,"So in the days of his mourning were past, Joseph spoke to the princes of Pharaoh, saying, If now I have found grace in your sight, speak in the hearing of Pharaoh, saying, My father made me swear, saying, Behold, in the grave I dug for myself in the land of Canaan, there you shall bury me."],[1756.1,"Now therefore let me go up and bury my father, and I will come back."],[1760.26,"Then Pharaoh said, Go up and bury your father as he made you swear."],[1764.74,"So Joseph went up to bury his father, and with him went up all the servants of Pharaoh, the elders of his house, and all the elders of the land of Egypt, as well as all the house of Joseph, his brothers, and his father's house."],[1777.38,"Only their sheep and oxen they left in the land of Goshen."],[1780.98,"There also went up with him both chariots and horses, and it was a very great gathering."],[1786.3,"Then they came to the threshing floor of Aad, which is beyond the Jordan, and they mourned there with a great and very solemn lamentation."],[1793.98,"The observed seven days of mourning for his father."],[1797.26,"So when the inhabitants of the land of Canaan saw the mourning at the threshing floor of Aad, they said, This is a deep mourning of the Egyptians."],[1805.02,"Therefore its name was called the Morning of Egypt, which is beyond the Jordan."],[1809.76,"So apparently this place was known by that name."],[1813.12,"This is the explanation."],[1814.4,"Oh, that's because Joseph showed up with his big Egyptian funeral procession there."],[1824.56,"Thus his sons did for him just as he commanded them, for his sons carried him to the land of Canaan and buried him in the cave of the field of Makhpala opposite Mamre, which Abraham bought from Ephron the Hittite as property for a burial place."],[1839.88,"After he buried his father, Joseph returned to Egypt, he and his brothers, and all who went up with him to bury his father."],[1847.08,"So this is clearly a story of his burial."],[1849.32,"Something to notice here, because it's going to be paralleled in Exodus, though, is part of why the first part of that was spelled out in detail, is that Joseph says to Pharaoh, I need to go here, I need to bury my father, and then I'll come back."],[1865.88,"Pharaoh says, Go do it."],[1867.96,"In Exodus, when Moses first comes to Pharaoh, his request is going to be not you need to let us all leave, but we need to go out of the desert to worship our God, and then we'll come back."],[1883.6,"And Pharaoh gives a very different answer."],[1886.02,"So we're given we're being given some of these things still at the end here of Genesis to see the difference in Exodus."],[1897.8,"And how things have changed."],[1904.6,"Verse 15. When Joseph's brothers saw their father was dead, they said, Perhaps Joseph will hate us and may actually repay us for all the evil we did to him."],[1913.88,"So they still have guilty consciences."],[1916.68,"Probably partially because, you know, their dad felt that. the need to rehearse all right before he died"],[1924.88,"So they came to Joseph, saying, Before your father died, he commanded, saying, Thus you shall say to Joseph, I beg you forgive the injustice of your brothers and their sin, for they did evil to you."],[1936.08,"Now forgive the injustice of the servants of the God of your father."],[1940.88,"And Joseph wept when they spoke to him."],[1943.12,"Then his brothers also went and fell down before his face, and they said, Behold, we are your servants."],[1948.88,"So Joseph said to them, Do not be afraid, for I belong to God."],[1953.36,"But as for you, you meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, in order to bring it about as it is this day to save many people alive."],[1962.72,"Now therefore do not be afraid, I will provide for you and your households."],[1964.48,"We'll pause there"],[1967.08,"Thus he comforted them and spoke to their heart."],[1972.2,"Thus he comes to them and spoke to their heart."],[1975.24,"So they just want to make clear."],[1978.65,"Hey, no hard feelings about that whole selling you into slavery and wanting to murder you thing."],[1984.26,"Like, we're all good."],[1985.7,"But so notice what Joseph says."],[1989.38,"He says, Look, I belong to God."],[1992.74,"Uh you guys weren tr'tying to do anything good."],[1995.56,"But God has brought good out of it."],[1999.66,"God has taken your evil intent and brought about good, as the ultimate result."],[2007.49,"He's not saying, therefore, that's okay."],[2012.18,"He's not saying, we'll just forget it ever happened."],[2015.28,"But he is saying, I belong to God."],[2019.43,"So he's saying, I'm on the same page as God."],[2022.95,"We're gonna bring good out of this."],[2024.57,"Therefore, I have goodwill toward you."],[2027.89,"This is an image of what forgiveness is."],[2031.33,"But this is this is gonna be an important theme throughout the Hebrew Bible, really into the New Testament, really the whole Bible."],[2043.14,"Is that this is part of the theodicy of the Hebrew Bible."],[2046.74,"of Theodicy being the question, you know, why does God let there be evil in the world?"],[2057.74,"Why does God allow human evil?"],[2059.98,"Which is really a question of why does God allow humans free will."],[2063.44,"Why does God allow humans agency?"],[2067.2,"And this is the fundamental answer of the Hebrew Bible is that God can take human evil, no matter how evil it is, even demonic evil."],[2080.36,"It's even used to explain why there are demons allowed to do things in the world and bring good out of it."],[2088.88,"And bring good out of it."],[2090.32,"it Which means he can't allow."],[2090.8,"Which means he can allow us to be free to love him"],[2097.64,"And also to be free not to."],[2102.28,"Because even a group of nomads who get jealous and decide to murder their brother, God can use that to save thousands and thousands of people's lives."],[2115.64,"Which is what just happened here."],[2117.24,"And what Joseph is pointing out."],[2121.08,"This sort of vile evil pettiness."],[2124.32,"God used how many people are alive now."],[2130.82,"And so for Joseph, sort of the glory and beauty of what God has done in saving all these lives is so much bigger and more important and more worthy of giving thanks to God than his need for vengeance and to be equally petty."],[2152.32,"And equally violent with his brothers."],[2154.64,"That why would I even dwell on that?"],[2160.66,"Why would I even dwell on that?"],[2163.14,"So let's finish up here."],[2168.1,"So Joseph dwelt in Egypt, he and his brothers."],[2170.98,"Then Joseph lived one hundred and ten years."],[2174.58,"Joseph saw Ephraim's children to the third generation."],[2178.58,"And the the children of Mekir, son of Manasseh, were also brought up on Joseph's knees."],[2187.18,"This becomes emblematic throughout the Hebrew Bible."],[2191.66,"This is the blessed life, is when you get to see your children's children."],[2197.18,"You've been blessed to have this long life."],[2199.02,"You get to see your children, you get to watch them grow up and become adults and have their own children and watch those children grow up."],[2215.5,"To the land God swore to our fathers Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob."],[2219.02,"Jacob. Because has been added to his people"],[2221.86,"This is, by the way, the first time that phrase has occurred."],[2230.18,"Thus Joseph took an oath from the children of Israel, saying, God will surely visit you, and you shall carry up my bones from here."],[2238.34,"So Joseph died being 110 years old, and they embalmed him and put him in a coffin in Egypt."],[2245.86,"So he gets the same promise."],[2249.06,"He says, I'm so sure that God is going to do this, is going to bring you out of Egypt."],[2256.66,"This isn't literally his brothers."],[2258.26,"Some of his brothers probably predeceased him."],[2260.34,"He was one of the younger brothers."],[2261.54,"This is talking about the whole family."],[2262.82,"I'm so sure this is going to happen that God's going to bring you back to Canaan"],[2263.94,"I want you to take my bones with you"],[2271.1,"So I can be added to my people when you go, even if it may be a long time, and it's going to be a long time."],[2278.38,"So that's where Genesis ends."],[2281.1,"As our lead-in to Exodus."],[2283.9,"And when we start Exodus next time, we'll see it picks up in a much worse spot."],[2289.34,"Things are not so nice in Egypt, uh, particularly between Pharaoh and the descendants of Israel."],[2298.54,"So that's it for tonight."],[2300.38,"We're obviously not starting on Exodus, but thank you, everybody."],[2305.66,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2313.02,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2314.14,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaithcom."]],"o":[{"t":20.4,"lv":2,"h":"49:1 - \"The last days\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:1</b> Jacob gathers sons: tell you what befalls you in <b>the last days</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Accurately translated from the Greek - but readers think <b>second coming</b>, Armageddon, end of the world</li><li class=\"d1\">\"clearly not talking about the end of the world\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Better: <b>latter days</b> = \"not tomorrow, down the road\"</li><li class=\"d1\">people avoid it \"because of the <b>Mormons</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":69.26,"lv":2,"h":"49:3-7 - Reuben, Simeon and Levi","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:3-4</b> <b>Reuben</b>: firstborn, might, beginning of children</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>hard to bear</b>, hardened in self-will, <b>unstable as water</b></li><li class=\"d1\">went up to father's bed, <b>defiled it</b> - \"kind of happened\"</li><li class=\"d1\">about the son, but also <b>character traits</b>: stubborn, strong-willed; see tribe of Reuben later</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:5-7</b> <b>Simeon and Levi</b>: injustice from free choice</li><li class=\"d1\">slew a man, <b>hamstrung an ox</b>; \"cursed be their anger\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>divide them in Jacob, scatter in Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sounds mean - refers to <b>Shechem</b> again</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: Shechem bad again? - yes</li><li class=\"d0\">Now past the <b>disinherited</b></li></ul>"},{"t":150.66,"lv":2,"h":"49:8-9 - Judah the lion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:8</b> Judah: brothers will <b>praise</b> you; hand on neck of enemies; father's sons <b>bow down</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:9</b> <b>lion's cub</b>, grown from a shoot; sleeps like a lion - <b>who shall rouse him?</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers bowing = <b>Joseph's dream</b> - no prophecy \"founded in the will of man\" (<b>St Peter</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">Judah has <b>firstborn status</b>, whether Jacob designates it or not</li><li class=\"d1\">plays out in the OT</li><li class=\"d0\">Lots of <b>animal imagery</b>: <b>ox</b> (Simeon, Levi), lion</li></ul>"},{"t":231.02,"lv":3,"h":"Animals and the zodiac","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Comment: related to the <b>Zodiac</b> - agreed</li><li class=\"d0\">Each constellation, as Hebrews understood it, lined up with <b>one of the twelve tribes</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Symbols present <b>literally</b>: <b>high priest's ephod</b> stones with constellations on them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Astrology bad\" / \"astrology dumb\" in modern world</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>newspaper astrology</b> mostly dumb, not so much evil - \"like a fortune cookie\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No real <b>astronomy</b> in the ancient world as we know it - the issue differs from what we think</li></ul>"},{"t":315.45,"lv":3,"h":"Jewish astrology vs pagan astrology","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Everyone in ancient world: sun, moon, stars <b>divine</b>, small-g <b>gods</b>, even Jews</li><li class=\"d1\">stars = <b>angels</b>, spiritual beings, through NT and <b>Revelation</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Philo of Alexandria</b> (1st c. BC): difference between <b>Moses and you pagans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">pagans think heavenly bodies <b>ultimate, worshipped, control destiny</b> = occult astrology</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses: they're <b>angels, messengers, servants of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jewish astrology</b>: God can <b>communicate</b> through the heavens</li><li class=\"d1\">e.g. <b>Messiah's birth</b> via a star in a certain constellation at a certain time</li><li class=\"d1\">not that the star was a god that caused it - <b>communication, messenger</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Psalm 19</b>: \"heavens proclaim the glory of God\" - literal astrological terms, horizon, zodiac</li></ul>"},{"t":466.96,"lv":3,"h":"Tribes and the heavens","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Twelve tribes tied to constellations: God's people <b>part of the workings of the cosmos</b></li><li class=\"d1\">comment: like \"stars of the heavens\" blessing</li><li class=\"d0\">Not supposed to <b>worship</b> them or think they <b>interpret destiny</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"God could speak through his creation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Astrology all over the OT: <b>Ezekiel's vision</b> of four living creatures - <b>Babylonian astrology</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Symbols similar not identical: <b>Leo</b> same lion; <b>Scorpio</b> often a <b>dragon</b></li><li class=\"d1\">freedom in interpreting</li><li class=\"d0\">So the <b>lion</b> becomes Judah</li></ul>"},{"t":558.27,"lv":2,"h":"49:10-12 - Scepter and Shiloh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:10</b> <b>scepter shall not depart from Judah</b> nor lawgiver until <b>Shiloh</b> comes; <b>expectation of the nations</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:11</b> binding <b>colt to a vine</b>, donkey's colt to branch; <b>washes garments in wine</b>, clothes in <b>blood of grapes</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:12</b> eyes gladdened with wine, teeth whiter than milk</li></ul>"},{"t":586.31,"lv":3,"h":"A messianic prophecy tied to Judah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not the first: first = <b>Genesis 3</b>, <b>seed of the woman</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"interesting since women don't have seed\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Identifies him with Judah</b> for the first time</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Mashiach</b> = anointed one, the king; <b>scepter</b> all over</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Shiloh</b> = a place (where <b>Samuel</b> will be) - \"until a city comes?\" - weird</li><li class=\"d0\">Read as <b>coming of Messiah</b>, then <b>second coming</b></li><li class=\"d1\">interpreted via <b>Psalm 110</b> (a couple years away)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Building block</b>: understanding of God and Messiah built before Exodus</li></ul>"},{"t":683.34,"lv":3,"h":"Q: Vine, colt and garments","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: what do vine and branch mean? (Jesus' entry)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cryptic</b> at the time - later prophet (<b>Zechariah</b>) does something with it</li><li class=\"d1\">king <b>riding a donkey's colt</b> he ties up himself</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>royalty and humility</b> \"two things that do not normally go together\"</li><li class=\"d1\">beyond that, no clear direct meaning - poetic, imagery that doesn't fit</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Wash in wine</b> - royal purple? but says <b>wash</b>, not dye</li><li class=\"d1\">\"you don't wash by putting wine on it - we'd call that a stain\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ambiguous double meaning: <b>blood</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Juxtapositions that don't logically fit together</li></ul>"},{"t":819.3,"lv":3,"h":"Emmaus: why it was cryptic","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Road to Emmaus</b>: Christ explains things in all the Scriptures concerning himself</li><li class=\"d1\">overplayed idea: no one could have understood the Messiah in the OT until Jesus</li><li class=\"d1\">\"bad news, a lot of people did\" - read <b>Second Temple literature</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Idea: once you see <b>who Christ is and what he does</b>, weird juxtapositions make sense</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>humility</b> + kingship; <b>Christ's blood</b> on garments; divine nature and <b>humiliation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"it all comes together\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Here it's \"almost a riddle\"</li><li class=\"d1\">historical <b>Judah</b> had no idea of details - just \"a <b>long dynasty of kings</b>, groovy\"</li></ul>"},{"t":950.71,"lv":2,"h":"49:13-15 - Zebulun and Issachar","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:13</b> <b>Zebulun</b>: dwell by the <b>sea coast</b>, haven for ships, border to <b>Sidon</b></li><li class=\"d1\">just told where descendants will live - \"short end of the deck\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:14-15</b> <b>Issachar</b> desired what was good; saw land fertile → <b>shoulder to hard work, a farmer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"levels of excitement\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: connects to <b>Ezra-Nehemiah</b> (helpers made Issachar)? - yes, why they picked Issachar; also where they dwelt, <b>farmland</b></li><li class=\"d0\">After nomadic life, <b>land to possess and hand down</b> = real promise</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>seacoast and ports</b> also legitimate</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not as exciting as having the Messiah\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1053.89,"lv":2,"h":"49:16-18 - Dan","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:16</b> <b>Dan</b> shall judge his own people</li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew <b>Dan = judge/judgment</b> - condemnation, not equity</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:17</b> <b>serpent</b>, viper in ambush, bites horse's heels, rider falls backward</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what'd I do?\" - about the <b>tribe</b>, \"nothing good\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Samson</b> - church fathers' view (people get upset)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Dan always a problem</b>: left out of the <b>new heavens and new earth</b> in Revelation - \"final word on you\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:18</b> waiting for the Lord's salvation</li></ul>"},{"t":1146.13,"lv":2,"h":"49:19-21 - Gad, Asher, Naphtali","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:19</b> <b>Gad</b>: raider gang raids him, he raids them in pursuit</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a <b>pirate's life</b> for you\" - live by wits, fight neighbors</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:20</b> <b>Asher</b>: abundant food, <b>dainties for rulers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"another great translation\" - \"let us all go and sup on dainties\"</li><li class=\"d1\">abundant food, delicacies = promise</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:21</b> <b>Naphtali</b>: spreading stem, bestowing <b>beauty</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"nice things\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1193.62,"lv":2,"h":"49:22-26 - Joseph","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:22</b> Joseph a <b>grown-up son</b>, envied; \"O my youngest son, returned to me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">evil plans, archers; <b>bows broken</b>, sinews enfeebled by the <b>hand of the Mighty One of Jacob</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:25-26</b> God of your father helps, blesses with <b>blessing of heaven above</b> and earth; <b>breasts and womb</b></li><li class=\"d1\">stronger than <b>everlasting hills</b>; on head of Joseph, <b>crown of the brothers he led</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"No favoritism things\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Recounted in front of the brothers who did it</li><li class=\"d0\">Again note <b>Ephraimite traditions</b> maintained here</li></ul>"},{"t":1264.45,"lv":2,"h":"49:27 - Benjamin","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:27</b> <b>Benjamin</b> a <b>ravenous wolf</b>: morning eats, evening provides food</li><li class=\"d1\">\"what did I do?\" - about <b>descendants</b>, a \"particularly sinister lot\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sinister joke on purpose</b>: most of the tribe <b>left-handed</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Benjamin = son of my right hand</b> - joke in the text</li><li class=\"d1\">\"take issue with <b>Moses</b> first\"; like <b>Sisyphus</b> jokes</li><li class=\"d0\">See what happens with Benjamin later</li></ul>"},{"t":1343.43,"lv":3,"h":"Judah/Benjamin vs. Joseph traditions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What's said of <b>Judah and Benjamin</b> explained by later history from Judah's perspective</li><li class=\"d0\">What's said of <b>Joseph</b> is <b>not</b> from that perspective</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Earlier Ephraimite traditions</b> held in parallel with Judah and Benjamin traditions</li><li class=\"d0\">→ pointer to <b>antiquity of the core</b> of the text</li></ul>"},{"t":1382.09,"lv":2,"h":"49:28-32 - Charge to bury him at Machpelah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:28</b> these are the <b>twelve sons of Israel</b>; blessed each by own blessing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:29-30</b> \"<b>I am to be added to my people</b>\" - bury with fathers in cave in field of <b>Ephron the Hittite</b> opposite <b>Mamre</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the tomb <b>Abraham bought</b>; Joseph already promised to return his body there</li></ul>"},{"t":1421.09,"lv":3,"h":"\"Added to my people\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Some (e.g. <b>Bart Ehrman</b>) say <b>resurrection / afterlife</b> a Christian invention; Israelites didn't believe - \"Read the Torah, Bart\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Beyond Isaac's language: <b>\"rest with my fathers\"</b> (could be metaphor - body next to body)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Added to my people</b> - recurs in <b>Kings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they are <b>somewhere</b>; \"I am going there to join them\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not subtracted from you, <b>added to them</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Antiquity</b> of the idea</li><li class=\"d0\">He sees death as <b>rejoining his people</b>: father, grandfather, mother, grandmother, <b>wives</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ wants body buried with them</li></ul>"},{"t":1530.58,"lv":3,"h":"Why Orthodox don't cremate","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q often asked: why <b>no cremation</b> in the Orthodox Church</li><li class=\"d1\">because of <b>belief in resurrection</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"we're being <b>added to our people</b>\" - take our body and put it with them</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"one bright morning... <b>I'll fly away</b>\" - leave body and world behind</li><li class=\"d1\">if so, \"sure, take it and burn it, who cares?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1574.8,"lv":3,"h":"49:31-33 - Leah's burial; Jacob dies; pilgrimage","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:31</b> buried <b>Abraham and Sarah, Isaac and Rebekah, Leah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">notice: buried with <b>Leah</b>, <b>not Rachel</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>49:33</b> feet up in bed, <b>breathed his last</b>, added to his people</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Place made very clear</b> in Genesis; Rachel buried separately, place known</li><li class=\"d0\">People <b>go there</b> on <b>pilgrimage</b> and pray - still do, from <b>three religions</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Relics, shrines</b>, praying at burial places - \"not a new thing in Christianity\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"definitely not in medieval Roman Catholicism\" - <b>embedded in the Torah</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Exodus: able to <b>return to places</b> where forefathers buried, <b>altars</b> to Yahweh</li><li class=\"d1\">\"we lost sense of <b>sacred places and sacred space</b> in Western culture\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1706.42,"lv":2,"h":"50:1-14 - Embalming and burial procession","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ch 50</b> Joseph falls on father's face, weeps, kisses</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Physicians embalm</b> Israel: <b>40 days</b>; Egyptians mourned <b>70 days</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Q: why embalm? - to take remains back to <b>Canaan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph asks <b>Pharaoh's princes</b> to ask leave: bury father as sworn, <b>I will come back</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh: \"Go up and bury your father\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Great procession: servants of Pharaoh, <b>elders of Egypt</b>, house of Joseph, <b>chariots and horses</b></li><li class=\"d1\">only sheep and oxen left in <b>Goshen</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Threshing floor of Atad</b> beyond the Jordan: <b>7 days</b> of lamentation</li><li class=\"d1\">Canaanites: \"deep mourning of the Egyptians\" → <b>Abel-mizraim</b>, \"mourning of Egypt\"</li><li class=\"d1\">explanation of an existing place name</li><li class=\"d0\">Sons bury him at <b>Machpelah</b>; return to Egypt</li></ul>"},{"t":1847.08,"lv":3,"h":"Foreshadowing of Exodus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Detail spelled out because it's <b>paralleled in Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph: \"I need to bury my father, <b>then I'll come back</b>\" → Pharaoh: \"Go do it\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Moses'</b> first request: go into the desert to <b>worship our God, then come back</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh gives \"a very different answer\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Shows <b>how things have changed</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1904.6,"lv":2,"h":"50:15-18 - The brothers' fear","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:15</b> brothers: \"Perhaps Joseph will <b>hate us</b>... repay us\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>guilty consciences</b>; dad felt the need to rehearse it before he died</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:16-17</b> message: \"<b>forgive the injustice</b> of the servants of the God of your father\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Joseph <b>wept</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers fall down: \"we are your <b>servants</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1948.88,"lv":2,"h":"50:19-21 - \"God meant it for good\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:19</b> \"Do not be afraid, <b>for I belong to God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:20</b> \"you meant evil... <b>God meant it for good</b>... to save many people alive\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:21</b> \"I will provide for you\" - comforted them, spoke <b>to their heart</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Brothers: \"no hard feelings about selling you into slavery and wanting to murder you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Joseph: <b>on the same page as God</b>; good will toward you</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"that's okay\", not \"forget it\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>An image of forgiveness</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2043.14,"lv":3,"h":"Theodicy: God brings good from evil","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Theme through the <b>Hebrew Bible and NT</b>; part of its <b>theodicy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why does God allow evil? = why does he allow <b>human free will/agency</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">Fundamental answer: God can take <b>any</b> human evil - even <b>demonic</b> - and <b>bring good out of it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even explains why <b>demons</b> are allowed to do things</li><li class=\"d0\">→ free to <b>love him</b>, and free <b>not to</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Nomads jealous, murder brother → God saves <b>thousands of lives</b></li><li class=\"d0\">For Joseph, glory of saving lives bigger than <b>need for vengeance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"why would I even dwell on that?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2163.14,"lv":2,"h":"50:22-26 - Joseph's death and oath","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:22</b> Joseph dwelt in Egypt, lived <b>110 years</b></li><li class=\"d1\">saw <b>Ephraim's children to third generation</b>; children of <b>Machir</b>, son of Manasseh, on his knees</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>blessed life</b> in Hebrew Bible: see <b>children's children</b>, watch them grow</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:24</b> \"God will surely visit you\" - bring you to land sworn to <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:25</b> oath: \"<b>carry up my bones</b> from here\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not literally his brothers (some predeceased); the whole family</li><li class=\"d1\">so sure God will bring them back to Canaan</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>50:26</b> dies at 110, <b>embalmed</b>, put in a <b>coffin in Egypt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"so I can be added to my people\" - \"a long time\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2278.38,"lv":3,"h":"End of Genesis; lead-in to Exodus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Genesis ends as <b>lead-in to Exodus</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Exodus picks up \"in a much worse spot\": things not nice in Egypt, <b>Pharaoh and descendants of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not starting Exodus tonight</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next time: **Exodus** - picks up in a much worse spot, Pharaoh vs. Israel"});
